toke.c: pass a local copy of no_code, not the const global itself, by value.

A const global aggregate that holds pointers, passed by value, faults in the
virtual profile's code generation: the copy into the argument area is made by
memcpy with operands moved through integer registers, so they arrive untagged
(docs/ref/ISSUES.md C-77). In Perl 5.36.3 the one such call is the lexer's
bareword path for a word starting with "::" (::is, ::ok in the core tests),
which faulted in memcpy at compile time. A local copy, as yyl_keylookup
already makes of the same constant, is passed correctly. Behaviour is
unchanged.

diff --git toke.c toke.c
index ea99050..2fa8219 100644
--- a/toke.c
+++ b/toke.c
@@ -9009,8 +9009,13 @@ yyl_try(pTHX_ char *s)
         s++;
         OPERATOR(PERLY_COMMA);
     case ':':
-        if (s[1] == ':')
-            return yyl_just_a_word(aTHX_ s, 0, 0, no_code);
+        if (s[1] == ':') {
+            /* capstone: pass a local copy. A const global aggregate that
+               holds pointers, passed by value, faults in the virtual profile's
+               codegen (docs/ref/ISSUES.md C-77). */
+            struct code c = no_code;
+            return yyl_just_a_word(aTHX_ s, 0, 0, c);
+        }
         return yyl_colon(aTHX_ s + 1);
 
     case '(':
